      "symbol-n"
    ],
    "note": "A **sign** gives information that is there to be seen or read (*a road sign*), or shows that something is true (*a sign of rain*). A **signal** is a light, sound, or movement made to send a message or a warning at a particular moment (*the signal to start*). A **symbol** is a picture or shape that stands for an idea (*a heart is a symbol of love*)."
  },
  "usage_note": null,
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "Dark clouds are a sign for rain.",
      "correct": "Dark clouds are a sign of rain.",
      "note": "Use **of** after **sign** when one thing shows another: *a sign of rain*, *a sign of trouble*."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "There was no signal of him at the party.",
      "correct": "There was no sign of him at the party.",
      "note": "**No sign of** someone means they have not appeared; a **signal** is a light, sound, or movement that sends a message."
    }
  ],
